{
  "dom_id": "step-q97425",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n\u27e8x(t),y(t)\u27e9=x(0)y(0)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=5-3t.$",
  "worked_solution": "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $\u27e8\\cdot ,\\cdot \u27e9$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016p(t)\u2016=\\sqrt{\u27e8p(t),p(t)\u27e9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=5-3t,$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(0)=5,\\,p(2)=-1,\\,p(3)=-4.\n$$\n\nComputing $\u2016p(t)\u2016$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016p(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{\u27e8p(t),p(t)\u27e9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(0)p(0)+p(2)p(2)+p(3)p(3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(0)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}+[p(3)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+1+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{42}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
